  "answer": "Nothing changes in this NQ unit. Its own checks all pass: 67 pass and 1 skips, the Linux-only test, across the seven planned test files. The `provision --host` failure belongs to whoever owns commit 4e96047 (provision.mjs and test/provision.test.mjs), and they should open a separate unit for it. The likely cause is that provisionHost (provision.mjs:61) treats claude as not installed in the test's fake machine env, so the claude block is never written. Either the test's machine() should make claude look installed, or provisionHost should not depend on that check for this file. Deliver this unit with that one test marked as a known pre-existing failure.",
